    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "86e4e6e5_b1826417",
        "filename": "android/apex.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 94,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-30T13:57:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not aim for [], i.e. make it practically non-optional? Better clarity.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 94,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 94,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "eab12a5930c12968d7db68856215490fd67e8237",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c53a8cf_817d7261",
        "filename": "android/apex.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 94,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-01T02:22:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, that\u0027s too ambitious I think :) Then, we will have to add \u0027apex_available: [\":platform\"] to EVERY modules that will be part of the platform. That\u0027s too many.",
      "parentUuid": "86e4e6e5_b1826417",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 94,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 94,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "eab12a5930c12968d7db68856215490fd67e8237",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8a27274a_7d0149bf",
        "filename": "android/apex.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 94,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-01T14:17:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I\u0027ve misunderstood them - I thought they\u0027d only be applicable to modules with exposed APEX interfaces, i.e. where we have stubs{} in case of cc_library.\n\nIf not, do we want to specify this on all internal intermediate dependencies as well (regardless of default)? Isn\u0027t ordinary visibility better suited for them if they need to be restricted?",
      "parentUuid": "5c53a8cf_817d7261",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 94,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 94,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "eab12a5930c12968d7db68856215490fd67e8237",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f2eb1d77_660401d8",
        "filename": "android/apex.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 94,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-02T01:30:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "iicu, most modules are by default only available to \":platform\". That\u0027s why we have bunch of *_available(bool) props. If we\u0027d want to control availability to the platform, I\u0027d like to have \"platform_available(bool)\" for consistency, instead of putting pseudo apex \":platform\" in \"apex_available\".\n\nThe only reason for \":platform\" seems being able to replace \"no_apex:true\" with \"apex_available: [\":platform\"]\" until default value changes from [\":platform\", \":anyapex\"] to [\":platform\"].\n\nI agree with Martin that default should be changed to [] and deprecating \":platform\". But for now, having \":platform\" and \":anyapex\" as default is fine with me.",
      "parentUuid": "8a27274a_7d0149bf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 94,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 94,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "eab12a5930c12968d7db68856215490fd67e8237",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
